p apple pro  as well as others actually leak the  schematics showing off the specifics of  what we should expect pointing to  awesome details like the earpiece  speaker on the 14 pro models being three  times thinner than the current one but  the best thing that shrimp apple pro  leaked was the pill plus hole cut out on  the pro models which will finally be  replacing the notch that has stuck  around since the iphone 12 and based on  all the mock-ups done online of how it  would look as well as our own custom  renders made by renders by shailesh  which were based on shrimp's cads i  think the 14 pro models are gonna be the  most beautiful iphones we've seen in  years and the best part is that multiple  sources like ross young and mark german  totally agreed with shrimp's leaks which  basically confirms that this will be the  design that we see this year especially  since the actual display glass parts  have been leaked showing off the design  of each model which i'll get into in  just a moment and ross young even  recently released the official screen  sizes of the models showing that the 14  pro will have a slightly larger 6.12  inch display compared to 6.06 inches and  the 14 pro max will have a 6.69 inch  compared to 6.68 which means that each  one will be getting slightly taller with  slimmer bezels and we even recently  started to see aluminum mock models of  the entire iphone 14 lineup showing off  the four models as well as some major  differences on the back first of all the  camera bumps on the 14 pro models are  absolutely massive and that's because  we're expecting the biggest camera  update we've seen on the iphone ever but  before i get into that let's talk about  the lightning port situation yes at this  point we're already expecting usbc to  come next year with the iphone 15 lineup  so it might seem like everyone is going  to be holding off but that's not  actually true so let me explain why  first of all the majority of common  people don't really care about which  port comes on the iphone is usually just  the tech enthusiasts that care but  thankfully i believe that the lightning  port on the 14 pro models is actually  going to get a huge update this year  allowing it to transfer data at usb 3.0  speeds which will fix the biggest issue  people are having with the iphone 13  lineup which is of course the slow  transfer speeds so even though we're not  getting usb-c this year lightning will  at least be getting a big upgrade on the  pro models where it's going to matter  the most because of the significantly  upgraded cameras but wait the upgrades  don't stop there because we have even  more leaks concerning even better  features minshequil recently reported  that the front camera on all four of the  new iphone 14 models is gonna get an  upgrade to support auto focus and a  faster f 1.9 aperture which will give it  a few different benefits first of all  the faster f 1.9 aperture compared to  the current f 2.2 on the iphone 13  lineup means that the selfie camera will  take in quite a bit more light which  means better quality photos with less  noise especially in dim environments not  only that but the faster aperture also  increases the depth of field which  basically means that the background will  look more blurry and that will actually  help the software take better portrait  selfies with more accurate cutouts and  now the biggest differences we're  expecting are actually going to be  coming to the pro models so let's focus  on those in terms of the displays the  big difference we're expecting is that  the refresh rate will be able to go down  to 1 hertz which means that it should be  easy to support and always on display  which is what i've been asking for for  years and because we're finally ditching  the notch and getting the dual cutouts  the bezels on the pro models are going  to be thinner than ever before giving us  even more screen real estate and in  terms of performance we're expecting the  new high-end a16 chip to come to the pro  models which will be built on tsmc's 4  nanometer process being even more  efficient and more powerful and  hopefully apple gives it a better  cooling system potentially vapor chamber  cooling which apple has reportedly been  testing this year so hopefully we stop  having overheating issues while gaming  but the main revolutionary feature we're  expecting is a brand new 48 megapixel  main camera on the back which is the  main reason why the camera bumps are  absolutely massive on the pro models  compared to the regular ones and the  beauty of the 48 megapixel camera is  that it's gonna greatly increase the  quality due to using a new much larger  sensor and apple is rumored to be using  pixel binning for nighttime and dimly  lit photos to make sure it takes in the  most amount of light and because of the  48 megapixel sensor it's gonna shoot 8k  video which i think will blow away any  other ak video on the market because i  believe apple's going to be using pro  res to shoot 8k because the a15 chip  already comes with prores encoders and  decoders so the a16 will for sure as  well and the biggest worry people had  about ak video was the lack of usbc but  once again i believe the lightning port  will be getting upgraded to support  faster transfer speeds so it won't  really be that big of an issue this year  and even though this year's iphone 14  pro isn't getting a full redesign we are  still expecting it to come with titanium  instead of stainless steel which means  it could be getting a bit lighter while  also being very tough and along with all  the other upgrades we're expecting  updated specs like wi-fi 6e bluetooth  5.2 a new 5g rf chip that's more  efficient satellite connectivity better  speakers better microphones and more and  based on our own renders i believe a lot  of people are going to love the look of  the iphone 14 pro and pro max especially  if there's a chance it comes with the  new copper slash bronze color and 